1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,800
A camera can record an event without getting help to the right person.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:09,700
EduSphere Safety connects real video tracking to evidence, staff review, and a recorded response.

3
00:00:10,250 --> 00:00:14,143
Meta SAM three point one tracks people in a recorded clip.

4
00:00:14,143 --> 00:00:17,683
The edge agent checks the source and applies zone rules.

5
00:00:17,683 --> 00:00:19,807
Our API stores incidents and evidence.

6
00:00:19,807 --> 00:00:23,700
Local Meta Llama drafts a briefing, while staff control the response.

7
00:00:24,250 --> 00:00:29,956
This is the running Next.js console backed by our dot net API and PostgreSQL.

8
00:00:29,956 --> 00:00:33,217
We sign in as the school safety officer.

9
00:00:33,217 --> 00:00:37,700
The overview shows devices, monitoring coverage, and incidents for this school.

10
00:00:38,250 --> 00:00:42,067
The school configures a zone, schedule, confidence threshold, and persistence.

11
00:00:42,067 --> 00:00:45,120
This versioned bundle names SAM three point one.

12
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:49,700
Multiple frames must support the configured rule before it produces an event.

13
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:55,996
Here, Meta SAM three point one tracks real people in a twelve-second public OpenCV recording.

14
00:00:55,996 --> 00:00:59,826
These boxes and IDs came from an actual API call.

15
00:00:59,826 --> 00:01:05,188
All one hundred and twenty frames returned tracks, with eight IDs across the clip.

16
00:01:05,188 --> 00:01:11,700
Our edge agent checks the source and evaluates the tracks, producing six events for this demonstration zone.

17
00:01:12,250 --> 00:01:15,103
We select one actual SAM zone event.

18
00:01:15,103 --> 00:01:19,994
An explicit demo handoff sends it to the API and retries it.

19
00:01:19,994 --> 00:01:22,032
Both requests return one incident.

20
00:01:22,032 --> 00:01:25,700
The record retains model version SAM three point one.

21
00:01:26,250 --> 00:01:32,643
This is the same real clip, uploaded with the event through the evidence API.

22
00:01:32,643 --> 00:01:37,210
Playback uses an authorized, short-lived link, and access is logged.

23
00:01:37,210 --> 00:01:39,493
The recording gives staff context.

24
00:01:39,493 --> 00:01:42,690
Automatic live-camera clip extraction remains future work.

25
00:01:44,250 --> 00:01:47,372
Meta Llama drafts an incident briefing locally.

26
00:01:47,372 --> 00:01:51,385
It receives only authorized event metadata, with no video.

27
00:01:51,385 --> 00:01:56,737
The structured result gives staff a summary, review steps, and explicit unknowns.

28
00:01:56,737 --> 00:02:00,304
It cannot change the incident or take action.

29
00:02:00,304 --> 00:02:03,426
Staff verify the draft against the evidence.

30
00:02:04,250 --> 00:02:09,236
The officer acknowledges the incident, adds an investigation note, and resolves it.

31
00:02:09,236 --> 00:02:13,390
Each transition checks the current version to prevent conflicting updates.

32
00:02:13,390 --> 00:02:16,299
The database records the actor and activity.

33
00:02:16,299 --> 00:02:21,700
Acknowledgement cancels pending escalation, connecting this real video event to an accountable response.

34
00:02:22,250 --> 00:02:30,877
In production, a configured pool-zone event could route an urgent alert to a supervisor by phone, SMS, or a site alarm.

35
00:02:30,877 --> 00:02:36,218
This demo verifies local email pickup, escalation settings, and the evidence access log.

36
00:02:38,250 --> 00:02:43,816
Five hundred and eighteen dot net tests and six Python tests pass.

37
00:02:43,816 --> 00:02:46,134
This validates a recorded-clip workflow.

38
00:02:46,134 --> 00:02:51,700
Field accuracy, continuous cameras, automatic delivery, and production sign-in remain next steps.

39
00:02:52,250 --> 00:02:57,713
Built with Meta SAM and Llama, EduSphere Safety records the response.

40
00:02:57,713 --> 00:02:59,700
Staff remain in control.
